<h2>Now</h2>
<p>Hello! My name (as the URL so helpfully indicates) is Thadeus Smith. I am an educator, writer, and Wikipedia administrator from the Pacific Northwest, now living in Boston. I coach speech and debate and train the people who teach it.</p>

<h3>What I'm doing now</h3>
<p><b>Teaching.</b> I am the Director of Education at Lumos Debate, where I supervise the instructors teaching Public Forum Debate across Greater Boston and run monthly virtual tournaments for hundreds of students. I also still coach Congressional Debate and World Schools Debate for American Heritage School in Florida, remotely and at national circuit tournaments.</p>
<p><b>Editing.</b> I am the lead editor of Champion Briefs' monthly Public Forum brief, and I review research from a team of coaches to make sure every argument holds up.</p>
<p><b>Photographing.</b> I recently joined WikiPortraits, photographing authors at book festivals and conventions around Boston so that their Wikipedia articles have a freely licensed portrait.</p>
<p><b>Writing.</b> This website is also the home of my <a href="/writing">longer writing</a>. My interests are varied: I have written about film, competitive speech and debate, transgender youth, human rights, books, and Wikipedia.</p>

<p>This is a <a href="https://nownownow.com/about">now page</a>. If you have your own website, you should make one too.</p>
</article>
